  "notes": "Worn by the ex-DHL 777Fs: B-226Y on Commons (2025-04-28). B-226W (ex-G-DHMB, owned by DHL Express per airport-data.com) is probably the same but no dated photo was found: not tagged. Only one photo, the left side from well below: the right side isn't seen, so its titles are drawn on the left only (the white scheme's right side carries the same titles over the same stretch, likely here too). The forward speed lines are seen to x 0.34, where the engine hides them, and the aft ones from 0.58 (the wing hides the stretch between): not drawn across the hidden part. The nose lines are less certain (the fit is weakest round the nose). The red belly's edge follows BCS/standard's (DHL's own 777F scheme, which this keeps) and agrees with the photo's overlay. The fin mosaic is the white scheme's, the same tiles at the same places in this photo, its white tile here yellow (the fin's base). Colours by eye.",
  "history": "New in the LAX round (2026-11-20)."
